  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTION, MANAGEMENT &amp; RESOURCE USE OF BLACK BRANT HABITAT BAHIA SAN QUINTIN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will: 1) work to have 5,505.78 acres at Laguna Figueroa decreed as a Mexican Federal Critical Habitat; 2) implement bird and habitat monitoring on 11,610.78 acres in the Bahia San Quintin wetland complex; 3) conduct research to determine the carrying capacity of the sea grass beds in Bahia San Quintin; 4) establish an environmental education Wildlife Management Unit at Punta Mazo; and, 5) implement an environmental education program to promote habitat sustainability and train 50 local residents in conservation, management of natural resources and control of solid waste.</narrative>
  </description>
